lib/tile -- TILE Forth's source library=======================================`TILE' is the name of the Forth itself: Mikael Patel's C implementation ofForth-83, version 2.48, 1989.  It is not a graphics or windowing thing.  Thedirectory is called `tile' because that is the path compiled into`CMDS/forth', which looks here and at $TILEPATH.  *.f83      the Forth-83 source library.  Load `forth.f83' and it pulls in             the enumeration, bit-field and structure definitions after it;             the rest -- blocks, debugger, macros, multi_tasking, queues,             ranges -- load on their own.  TST/       the twenty-two programs it shipped with.  Each checks its own             answer and aborts with a message if it is wrong.A SOURCE FILE IS A COMMAND-LINE ARGUMENT:    cd /dd/lib/tile/TST    forth fibonacci.tst    20 fib . cr    bye`include' is defined in the library, not the kernel, so it works only afterthe library has been loaded.Manuals are in DOC/forth, one per library module, plus the tile(1) man page.The C source is in SRC/pd7, under the GPL; DOC/forth/COPYING is its licence.